SUMMARY:Vietnam & Cambodia with Angkor Wat! Ancient Kingdoms of Southeast 
 Asia!!
DESCRIPTION:20s 30s Toronto Social & Activities\nA Meetup trip in December
  . . . what can be a better gift for the holidays?! Join our travelers gro
 up on a captivating 14-day journey through the heart of Southeast Asia as 
 we explore the vibrant cultures and breathtaking landscapes of Vietnam & C
 ambodia (Dec 04-18\, 2026)\n\nAs with all our tailor-made Meetup trips\, o
 ur expert guides will lead us off the beaten path to uncover the authentic
  charm of each destination\, while comfortable accommodations and deliciou
 s local cuisine ensure a truly immersive travel experience. Embark on an u
 nforgettable journey through the vibrant cities and breathtaking landscape
 s of Vietnam\, finishing with the wonders of Cambodia.\n\nWe begin in Hano
 i\, where history and culture come alive\, then sail the emerald waters of
  Halong Bay. Step back in time among the imperial treasures of Hue\, wande
 r the lantern-lit streets of charming Hoi An\, and feel the dynamic energy
  of Ho Chi Minh City. We conclude your adventure at the awe-inspiring temp
 les of Siem Reap\, home to the legendary Angkor Wat.\n\nTRIP HIGHLIGHTS:\n
 \n* **Hanoi**\; explore Ho Chi Minh sites\, Temple of Literature\, Old Qua
 rter cyclo ride & water puppet show\n* Visit rural **craft villages**: con
 ical hat & incense making\, home-hosted lunch\, village walk\n* **Ha Long 
 Bay cruise**: limestone islands\, floating villages\, cave visit\, Tai Chi
  & sunset views\n* **Hue**: Perfume River boat ride\, Thien Mu Pagoda\, Kh
 ai Dinh’s Tomb & Imperial Citadel\n* Scenic **Hai Van Pass train** to Da
 nang\; explore Dragon Bridge\, Cham Museum\, Marble Mountain\n* **Hoi An A
 ncient Town** (UNESCO)\, visit tailor shops\, pottery village & organic fa
 rm with cooking class\n* **Ho Chi Minh City & Cu Chi Tunnels**\; War Remna
 nts Museum\, Reunification Palace & Ben Thanh Market\n* **Mekong Delta cru
 ise**: coconut workshops\, sampan ride\, orchards & lunch in riverside vil
 lage\n* **Siem Reap**: dinner with Apsara dance\, Angkor temples (Ta Prohm
 \, Bayon\, Angkor Wat)\n* Cambodian cultural immersion: **monk blessing**\
 , village crafts & cooking\, **Tonle Sap Lake sunset cruise**\n\nFor a det
 ailed Day By Day itinerary: **[Click Here](https://forms.gle/cQdqYw74gAYqp
 hXX8)**[ to fill out our info request form](https://forms.gle/cQdqYw74gAYq
 phXX8)\n\n*Trip Itinerary:*\n\n* **Hanoi** – 3 nights\n* **Ha Long Bay (
 cruise)** – 1 night\n* **Hue** – 2 nights\n* **Hoi An** – 2 nights\n
 * **Ho Chi Minh City** – 3 nights\n* **Siem Reap** – 3 nights\n\n**Pri
 ce per person\, double occupancy: US$4400**\n(we match roommates for those
  willing to share and save)\n**Price for single room: US$5300**\n\n**RSVP 
 with your email address to receive complete information and itinerary. To 
 secure your spot on this trip\, please submit a US$450 deposit.**\n[Click 
 Here for Secure Deposit Link](https://www.paypal.com/instantcommerce/check
 out/EM44C56V6RFTC)\nDeposit is refundable up to 90 days before the departu
 re (less PayPal fees)\n[Fill Out this FORM if you are making a deposit](ht
 tps://forms.gle/Tpz4v9jEbc13FSU38)\nLimited capacity of 24 total. This tri
 p will fill up extremely quickly.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Airfare from/to the US not
  included. Contact Anna for a quote\\*\\*\\***\n\n***[Click Here](https://
 secure.meetup.com/messages/?new_convo=true&member_id=131297062)***[ to Mes
 sage Direct to Anna.](https://secure.meetup.com/messages/?new_convo=true&m
 ember_id=131297062)\nShe can help you arrange the airfare and answer any l
 ogistics questions.\n\nWe believe in good decent social. This events is cr
 oss posted to several other groups and the number of RSVPs on each is not 
 reflective. We have a set of sister groups where we post our local free\, 
 local/regional camping\, and our overseas events too.\n[Click Here to see 
 all our other fun events](https://www.meetup.com/ccccc-c/events/)\n\nWe do
  a [monthly Zoom with Q & A ](https://www.meetup.com/moretoexplore/events/
 296044209/)on all our overseas events.\nCome to the zoom and ask any quest
 ions. Great way to get the info you want without all the other fluff. As w
 ell as meet us and other attendees.\n\n[Click here ](https://www.meetup.co
 m/MoreToExplore/events/282719353/)for General Policies and useful info abo
 ut our international trips.\n\nLive the adventure instead of only dreaming
  it!\n\nSOT 2000318-10
