SUMMARY:Unforgettable Croatia! The Pearls of the Dalmatian Coast - Split\,
  Dubrovnik..
DESCRIPTION:20s 30s Toronto Social & Activities\nJoin our Meetup group on 
 this exciting tour of beautiful Croatia - a country blessed with both\, tr
 ansparent sapphire waters and glamourous old towns. A blissful vacation to
  a country full of beauty and history with an awesome group of active and 
 fun people! Create lifelong friendships on our tours! *Come alone\, leave 
 with friends!*\n\nFrom north to south\, we will start with Croatia's charm
 ing capital\, Zagreb. Visit the amazing Plitvice Lakes National Park\, wit
 h its cascading waterfalls. Explore the former Roman citadel of Split with
  Diocletian's famous palace. Marvel at the UNESCO World Heritage city of D
 ubrovnik\, boasting the largest and best preserved city walls in Europe. C
 heck out the filming locations of Game of Thrones. Relax on Croatia's stun
 ning Dalmatian coast\, overlooking the crystal blue Adriatic Sea. Spend a 
 couple of days on the sun drenched islands of Hvar and Korčula. Be our ow
 n boat crew for a day\, while sailing to the famous Blue cave and 5 more i
 slands.\n\nFor a detailed Day By Day itinerary:\n**[Click Here](https://fo
 rms.gle/cQdqYw74gAYqphXX8)**[ to fill out our info request form](https://f
 orms.gle/cQdqYw74gAYqphXX8)\n\nThe trip cost includes:\n\n* 2 Nights Zagre
 b at Hotel Dubrovnik or similar\n* 2 Night Split at AC Hotel by Marriott o
 r similar\n* 2 Nights Hvar at Podstine Hotel or similar\n* 3 Nights Dubrov
 nik at Hotel Royal Neptunor similar\n* Arrival and Departure Transfers\n* 
 Transportation throughout the tour\n* Ferry tickets Hvar - Korcula - Dubro
 vnik\n* Boat Charter for a day with visits to the Blue Cave and 5 islands\
 n* Bus Transportation from Zagreb to Split\n* Plitvice Lakes National Park
  Tour\n* Zagreb Sightseeing and Tasting Tour\n* Split Walking Tour\n* Kor
 čula Wine and Food Tour\n* Dubrovnik Game of Thrones Tour\n* Daily Breakf
 ast\n* 3 dinners and 2 tasting menus\n\n*Not Included:*\nx Transatlantic A
 irfare (we can help you arrange that)\nx Meals or activities not listed ab
 ove\nx Tips and any personal and incidental expenses\n\n**Price per person
 \, double occupancy: US$4550**\n(we match roommates for those willing to s
 hare and save)\n**Price for single room: US$5750**\n\n**The only way to se
 cure your spot is a US$450 deposit**\n**[Click Here for Secure Deposit Lin
 k](https://www.paypal.com/instantcommerce/checkout/WLM7LYMKTD3BC)**\nDepos
 it is refundable up to 90 days before the departure (less PayPal fees).\n*
 [Click Here](https://forms.gle/CQiGWo6p7kgHKSSF6)* [and Fill out this Form
  if you are making a Deposit ](https://forms.gle/CQiGWo6p7kgHKSSF6)\n\nLim
 ited capacity of 20 total. This trip will fill up extremely quickly.\n**\\
 *\\*\\*Airfare from/to the US not included. Contact Anna for a quote\\*\\*
 \\***\n\n***[Click Here](https://secure.meetup.com/messages/?new_convo=tru
 e&member_id=131297062)***[ to Message Direct to Anna with any questions in
 cluding airfare quotes.](https://secure.meetup.com/messages/?new_convo=tru
 e&member_id=131297062)\nShe can help you arrange the airfare and answer an
 y logistics questions.\n\nWe believe in good decent social. This event is 
 cross posted to several other groups and the number of RSVPs on each is no
 t reflective.\n\n[Click Here](https://www.meetup.com/moretoexplore/events/
 297686993/)[ ](https://www.meetup.com/moretoexplore/events/313670972/)for 
 the main Meetup post of this event.\nStill have questions? We do a monthly
  [Q&A Travel Zoom](https://www.meetup.com/moretoexplore/events/296044209/)
  on all our events\nCome to the zoom and ask any questions. Great way to g
 et the info you want without all the other fluff. As well as meet us and o
 ther attendees.\n\n[Click here for General Policies](https://www.meetup.co
 m/MoreToExplore/events/282719353/) and useful info about our international
  trips.\n\nWe have a set of sister groups where we post our local free\, l
 ocal/regional camping\, and our overseas events too.\n[Click Here to see a
 ll our other fun events](https://www.meetup.com/CulturalArts/Events)\n\nLi
 ve the adventure instead of only dreaming it!\n\nSOT 2000318-10
